# **A reverse-charge invoice claimed as though the supplier had filed it** —
# Plan 123 Slice H.
#
# Under reverse charge the *recipient* pays the tax and takes the credit; the
# supplier declares no outward tax, so nothing arrives in GSTR-2B and nothing
# ever will. An RCM invoice sitting in the register with no self-assessment
# behind it is credit claimed on a liability nobody discharged.
#
# **This is the inverse of every "not filed" rule in this pack, and that is
# the point.** Those rules all *exclude* reverse charge — correctly, because
# an absent supplier line is expected there. The exclusion means the RCM case
# falls through every one of them and is checked by none. This rule exists to
# catch what the exclusions let past.
#
# The test is deliberately narrow: an RCM invoice that also appears in a 2B
# is the contradiction worth reporting, because the supplier has declared
# forward tax on a supply the recipient is self-assessing. One of the two
# treatments is wrong and both parties have acted on their own.

PREFIX gst: <https://graph-owl.dev/packs/gst#>

SELECT ?invoice ?number ?gstin ?taxAmount ?reverseCharge
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?register {
    ?canonical gst:recordedIn ?invoice .
    ?invoice a gst:PurchaseInvoice ;
             gst:issuedBy      ?supplier ;
             gst:invoiceNumber ?number ;
             gst:taxAmount     ?taxAmount ;
             gst:reverseCharge ?reverseCharge .
    ?supplier gst:supplierGstin ?gstin .
  }

  GRAPH ?authority {
    ?canonical gst:reflectedIn ?filed .
    ?filed a gst:Gstr2bInvoice .
  }

  FILTER (?reverseCharge = "Y")
}
ORDER BY ?number
